        "name": "Self-consistent EFC background (FLAT FRW)",
        "validity": "Background solver for FLAT FRW with the EFC action (eq. 1): alpha=0.01, k0=1.0, omega_crit=1000.0, gamma0=0.05, Omega_m=0.3, V0=0.7, nonminimal_sign=+1. This is the FIRST self-consistent EFC background: phi is driven by the flow condition (13), H by (12) and lambda is a response field (eq. 10). Boltzmann/CMB is OPEN — no perturbations, no EFCLASS. Valid only for rho_m < rho_crit (K diverges, eq. 2), for z where radiation is negligible, and with V = const chosen because the paper does not specify V(phi). Super-horizon and ADM stability are open in the paper.",
        "law_form": "3 M_Pl^2 F(phi) H^2 = rho_m + K phi_dot^2/2 + V(phi) + sigma 3 M_Pl^2 H F_dot + lambda_dot phi_dot (eq. 12); phi_ddot + 3 H phi_dot = Gamma(rho) (eq. 13); F = 1 + alpha phi; K = k0/(1 - rho/rho_crit) (eq. 2); Gamma per eq. 47 — sigma = +1 is the paper's printed form, -1 is the direct variation of eq. 1."
      },
      "phase": "computation_engine",
